### Reject unusable inspector ports during manifest parsing

**Severity:** `medium`

An explicit negative, zero, or over-65535 `debugPort` currently passes manifest validation and fails only when the extension is launched. Rejecting it here turns a delayed launch failure into a precise manifest error; please add regression cases for `-1`, `0`, and `65536`.

```suggestion
        // Rule 3: an explicit inspector port must be usable as a TCP port. Port 0 is not
        // supported because the host must know which port the extension selected.
        if (package.CmdPal.DebugPort is <= 0 or > 65535)
        {
            return JSExtensionManifestParseResult.Failure("The 'cmdpal.debugPort' field must be between 1 and 65535.");
        }

        // Rule 4: either cmdpal.main or top-level main must resolve to an existing file.
        var entryPoint = !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(package.CmdPal.Main)
            ? package.CmdPal.Main
            : package.Main;

        if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(entryPoint))
        {
            return JSExtensionManifestParseResult.Failure("Neither 'cmdpal.main' nor the top-level 'main' entry point was specified.");
        }

        var resolvedEntryPoint = ResolveEntryPoint(extensionDirectory, entryPoint!, out var resolutionError);
        if (resolvedEntryPoint is null)
        {
            return JSExtensionManifestParseResult.Failure(resolutionError!);
        }

        // Rule 5: Node must be able to run the entry point directly. Only .js, .mjs, and .cjs are
        // supported. Uncompiled .ts source is rejected.
        if (!IsSupportedEntryPointExtension(resolvedEntryPoint))
        {
            return JSExtensionManifestParseResult.Failure($"The entry point '{entryPoint}' must be a JavaScript file with a .js, .mjs, or .cjs extension.");
        }

        if (!File.Exists(resolvedEntryPoint))
        {
            return JSExtensionManifestParseResult.Failure($"The entry point '{entryPoint}' does not resolve to an existing file.");
        }

        // Rule 6: a symbolic link or junction must not redirect the entry point outside the extension
```

### Fail closed when an entry-point segment disappears

**Severity:** `high`

If a path segment disappears between the existence check and `GetAttributes`, this catch currently reports that the segment is safe. That makes a containment check fail open during a filesystem race; treat the unverifiable segment as unsafe and add a race-oriented regression test around the containment helper.

```suggestion
            // The entry point was present before validation began. If a segment disappears during
            // the walk, fail closed rather than trusting a path whose attributes were not verified.
            return true;
```

### Retry notification admission after the consumer wins the race

**Severity:** `medium`

The consumer can remove the last queued item after `TryWrite` reports full but before this `TryRead`. In that interleaving, returning here silently loses the new notification and does not increment `DroppedNotificationCount`; retry while the channel remains open.

```suggestion
            if (_notificationQueue.Reader.Completion.IsCompleted)
            {
                return;
            }

            Thread.Yield();
```

### Isolate disconnect event subscribers

**Severity:** `medium`

A throwing `Disconnected` subscriber currently prevents every later subscriber from observing teardown. Invoke subscribers individually and log failures so one consumer cannot disrupt the rest; please add coverage with a throwing first subscriber and an observing second subscriber.

```suggestion
            var handlers = Disconnected;
            if (handlers is null)
            {
                return;
            }

            foreach (EventHandler handler in handlers.GetInvocationList())
            {
                try
                {
                    handler(this, EventArgs.Empty);
                }
                catch (Exception ex)
                {
                    Logger.LogError("A JSON-RPC disconnected event handler failed.", ex);
                }
            }
```
